-- an untyped definition is not elaborated: a checked definition with a leading implicit parameter
-- applied to its explicit arguments only would take the first for the implicit one (A := #3);
-- refused with the remedy named. Passing every parameter in order, as untyped code does, is fine.
idw : {A : Type} → A → A
idw x = x
fine = idw Word #3
#same fine = #3
wrong = idw #3
